#
# ThreadSanitizer suppressions. Use with
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<repository>/tests/tsan.supp:...
# See "Sanitizers" in docs/testing.md. An entry needs a reason that holds for every
# report it can match, and nothing here may hide a race in this project's code.

# A worker thread posts work to the GUI thread with
#   QMetaObject::invokeMethod(context, [..]{ .. }, Qt::QueuedConnection)
# Qt builds the slot object (a QtPrivate::QCallableObject, a header template that is
# compiled into our code and so is instrumented) on the worker, queues it, and the
# GUI thread runs it. The queue is locked inside libQt6Core, which is not
# instrumented, so ThreadSanitizer never sees the lock that orders the worker's
# construction before the GUI thread's call and reports the slot object's own fields.
# The entry matches only reports where the earlier access is that constructor, that
# is, the object's own initialisation. A lambda body is not matched: its frames never
# include the constructor, so a race on data the lambda touches is still reported.
race:QtPrivate::QCallableObject<*>::QCallableObject(
